The Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in north-eastern South Africa and runs along the border with Mozambique to the east and Zimbabwe to the north, while the southern boundary is the Crocodile River.
The park covers 19,500 km2 and is divided into 14 different eco-zones, each of which supports different wildlife.
